Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. RENTED OFFICE - FRIDAY - DAY

The new beige estate's keys lie beside an isolated laptop. Original drive under Zoe's chair; working copy on the desk.

Zoe reads WHO RECEIVES A BRG CASE? She moves her hands off the keyboard.

ZOE
Not mine. Another one.

A different root links to RCP-0447. The lookup: RECEIVING CANDIDATE PROFILE.

Stable home, finance and tenure. Then exposure, disclosure, compliance, attachment, leverage, sponsor. Zoe's expression changes.

ZOE
They want good parents.

ELIAS
Stable households. Those aren't the same thing. Chaos draws attention.

A declined profile has high professional exposure and low compliance. Another household is APPROVED — NOT MATCHED, without a child attached. RCP-0447 specifies capacity one, age six to nine, permanent, before its case link. A completed match clears a numeric threshold.

ZOE
They profile the adults too. Being here doesn't prove what they knew.

She writes: FIND OUT WHAT THEY WERE TOLD.

INT. VOSS AND VALE'S ROOM - SAME DAY

Vale remembers a normal house, family photographs and a woman kneeling to the arriving girl and crying.

VALE
I thought relief. It isn't evidence of what she knew.

They trace adult property and sponsor records, not the child's school, medical history or public identity.

INT. RENTED OFFICE - LATER

Motive codes have no readable definitions. They leave them unresolved. A match-summary database might contain private child records.

ZOE
Don't open the rows. Fields only.

Schema columns: age fit, sex fit, physical characteristics, behaviour, medical, history, preference, attachment, score.

She snaps the laptop closed and walks around the table.

ZOE
They shop. And call it safeguarding.

ELIAS
What do you want to do?

ZOE
Stop. For today. Tomorrow we don't open those rows either.

He nods until she tells him to stop nodding. A brief laugh breaks through.

INT. BEIGE ESTATE/INN - LATER

Cake boxes between them. Zoe thinks of Helen cutting labels from shirts, Brian at a school play — no verdict attached to these ordinary memories.

ZOE
They'd score well. High attachment.

ELIAS
Nothing there tells us what they knew.

She adds a new rule: PRIVATE ISN'T AUTOMATICALLY EVIDENCE.

They list compartments, real infrastructure and convincing paper.

ELIAS
People assuming somebody else checked.

She underlines it. Then closes the notebook.

ZOE
Years of monitor. What woke my case up on Monday?
